}

clarity_hierarchy.raw_response:
{
"critique":"The central modal panel creates a 'box within a box' hierarchy that traps the primary focal point (the title) and forces the eye to work through a container before reaching the content. The START button, while high contrast, is visually disconnected from the title by the instructions line, breaking the natural Title -> Action reading flow. The pixel skier, a key narrative element, is buried in the lower third and partially obscured by the modal's shadow, making it a tertiary element rather than a co-lead. The instructions line is a single, flat string of text that lacks visual grouping, making it harder to parse quickly. The top-left 'POWDER SOFT' and top-right 'SND ON' elements are too small and low-contrast to be clearly readable, creating visual noise without clear hierarchy.",
"suggestion":"1. Remove the heavy modal container and let the title, instructions, and button float directly over the scene to reduce visual nesting. 2. Increase the scale of the START button and move it closer to the title to create a tighter, more dominant primary action cluster. 3. Group the instructions into distinct visual chunks (e.g., icons for 'Steer' and 'Dodge') to improve scannability. 4. Reposition the skier to be more prominent, perhaps larger or in a clearer area of the slope, to establish a stronger connection between the character and the game world. 5. Increase the size and contrast of the top HUD elements to make them legible and part of the overall hierarchy."
}

