  "suggestion": "1. **De-modalize the UI:** Remove the dark box. Integrate the title and instructions directly into the sky or as a 'scoreboard' style HUD at the top, allowing the full slope to be visible. 2. **Scale the Hero:** Enlarge the pixel skier significantly and place them in the foreground (bottom center or right), perhaps mid-turn, to create a sense of motion and scale. 3. **Enhance the Snow:** Add pixel-level texture to the snow (light blue shadows, white highlights) to suggest depth and 'powder' quality. 4. **Vibrant Palette:** Shift the sky from muddy purple to a deep, rich indigo or midnight blue with brighter, distinct stars to increase contrast and 'crispness.' 5. **Arcade Title Treatment:** Give the 'SKIFREE' text a heavy, multi-layered pixel drop-shadow or a 'glitch' effect to make it pop against the sky, mimicking classic arcade cabinet aesthetics."
}

